cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Roomsmith: an open-source AI interior design agent"
message: "If you use Roomsmith in your work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Suseenthiran Arulraj
    family-names: Rumeasiyan
    alias: Rumeasiyan
repository-code: "https://github.com/Rumeasiyan/roomsmith"
url: "https://github.com/Rumeasiyan/roomsmith"
abstract: >-
  Roomsmith turns photographs of a real room into scaled floor plans, wall elevations, isometric
  cutaways, photoreal renders and a client-ready design report in which every change carries a
  specification, a design reason and a validation against the room's constraints. Geometry is
  computed from a single room model rather than generated, so drawings cannot invent an opening or
  misrepresent a room's size; those drawings are then used to constrain the image model. It runs as
  a team of six agents with approval gates so nothing expensive happens without a human decision.
keywords:
  - interior design
  - artificial intelligence
  - ai agents
  - multi-agent systems
  - architectural drawings
  - floor plans
  - generative design
  - design automation
  - image generation
